+"""Native parser for HDF4 Scientific Data Sets (the SD interface used by MODIS and most NASA
+HDF4 products), producing virtual references without decoding any data.
+
+HDF4 (unlike HDF5) is a flat list of *data descriptors* (tag, ref, offset, length). The SD
+interface groups the pieces of each dataset in a Vgroup of class ``Var0.0``:
+
+* ``SD``  (tag 702) - the data element: plain (contiguous, uncompressed bytes) or "special"
+  (tag | 0x4000): compressed (``SPECIAL_COMP``) or chunked (``SPECIAL_CHUNKED``, with a chunk
+  table stored as a Vdata and one ``CHUNK`` element per chunk, each optionally compressed);
+* ``NT``  (106) - number type (dtype and byte order); ``SDD`` (701) - rank and shape;
+* ``VH``/``VS`` (1962/1963) Vdatas of class ``Attr0.0`` - attributes;
+* Vgroups of class ``Dim0.0`` - the dimensions (their names are the HDF4 dimension names).
+
+File attributes are ``Attr0.0`` Vdatas attached to the ``CDF0.0`` root Vgroup. NASA products
+put their ODL metadata (``CoreMetadata.0`` etc.) there; it is flattened into attributes.
+
+Only DEFLATE-compressed or uncompressed storage can be referenced; other HDF4 codings (RLE,
+N-bit, Skipping Huffman, SZIP, JPEG), linked-block and external storage raise
+``NotImplementedError`` for that variable (use ``skip_variables``).
+
+Reference: *HDF Specification and Developer's Guide* (The HDF Group), chapters on data
+descriptors, Vgroups/Vdatas, special elements and the SD model. The tag-walking logic
+follows the (MIT-licensed) experimental reader in kerchunk (``kerchunk.hdf4``), re-implemented
+here without kerchunk or fsspec, reading through the ObjectStoreRegistry.
+"""
